### MODEL (turn 3)
Fixed the single-decimal bug in `parse_amount` in `ledger/money.py`: the fractional part is now padded to two digits before conversion, so `10.5` books 1050 cents instead of 1005. The existing tests pass, and spot checks confirm `10.5`, `10.50`, `10`, `10.`, `0.5`, and `-3.07` all parse correctly. Public names and signatures are unchanged.
